// DELIBERATELY BROKEN: two theorems cite each other, so neither can ever be proved.
//
// Before cycle detection this file printed `OK: 0 theorems proven` and exited 0 — the
// engine parked both proofs, drained its run queue, and returned as if quiescent. Nothing
// examined the parked set, so "no theorems were proved" was reported as success. Silence
// must never imply verification: a wedge is now a hard error naming every participant.
//
// (A SELF-citation is caught earlier and differently, by the read pass — see
// `cites '<name>', whose proof has not completed`. This file is the ≥ 2 case, which
// reaches the engine's wait-for graph instead.)
pred p

theorem first: p
proof
  @conclusion |
    p
    [by cite second]
qed

theorem second: p
proof
  @conclusion |
    p
    [by cite first]
qed
